{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.RemainderModule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.RemainderModule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Infix","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.isNormalForm","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/remainder-module.lean#L30-L37","doc":"An element is in **normal form** w.r.t. a rewriting system if no\nrule's leading monomial appears as a subword of any monomial in\nthe element's support. This characterizes elements of Õ(I).\nSee `QOU.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm` (proved, no sorry). ","signatureChunk":0}]}